    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and produces trustworthy performance measurements. It assumes a serving stack with a scheduler, one or more model replicas spanning multiple nodes/devices, a request ingress path, and observability plumbing.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every rank/node is running the model and serving configuration you think it is.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash verification.** Every node loads weights from a canonical, content-addressed source. Record the SHA-256 (or equivalent) of the weight files, tokenizer files, and config files at load time and assert all ranks report identical hashes. Mismatched shards across TP ranks is a classic silent-corruption failure.\n- [ ] **Tokenizer identity.** Confirm tokenizer version/vocab hash matches across nodes and matches the model's training tokenizer. Log `vocab_size` as loaded vs. `config.vocab_size` \u2014 embedding sharding bugs surface here.\n- [ ] **Config provenance.** Capture the full resolved serving config (max context length, max batch size, KV-cache budget per device, quantization settings, dtype, rope scaling, sampling defaults) as a single serialized artifact. Diff it against the intended config; reject startup on unexplained drift.\n- [ ] **Dtype and quantization audit.** Per-rank check: actual compute dtype, weight dtype, KV-cache dtype. Verify quantization (if any) applied the same group sizes/scales on every rank. A single rank running FP16 while others run BF16 will produce plausible-but-wrong outputs.\n- [ ] **Parallelism topology confirmation.** Log world size, TP/PP/EP/DP degrees, and the rank\u2192(node, device) mapping. Verify it matches",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
